b. View and read the source code for personal study and to understand how
   Rola works.

2. What you may not do

Unless you have written permission from the author, you may not:

a. Copy, redistribute, sublicense, or sell Rola or any substantial part of it.

b. Publish, host, or distribute a modified version of Rola, or create and
   distribute an app or website based on it.

c. Use Rola or any part of it for commercial purposes. This includes selling
   it, including it in a paid product or service, adding advertising, or
   offering it as a paid or hosted service.

d. Remove or alter the copyright notice or this license.

e. Use the Rola name or the author's name to promote or endorse another
   product or service.

Making this repository public allows GitHub users to view and fork it through
GitHub, as described in GitHub's Terms of Service. It does not grant permission
to redistribute, publish, sell, or commercially use Rola outside the rights
listed in this license.

3. Asking for permission

If you want to use Rola in a way that is not allowed above, open an issue in
this repository or contact the author through his GitHub profile. Please
describe what you want to use and how you plan to use it.

